Flint serving on the B70 guest (installed from b70-inference/scripts/flint-vllm-xpu/serve/).

  flint-inference.service  vLLM XPU + DFlash 2 (k=4), :8080, enabled at boot
  flint-llamacpp.service   llama.cpp rollback, :8080, disabled; Conflicts= with the above

API key: /etc/b70-flint/api-key (root 0600) -> systemd credential -> VLLM_API_KEY env.
flint_auth.FlintAuth requires `Authorization: Bearer <key>` on all routes except /health
(and /metrics from loopback).

Rollback:   sudo systemctl disable --now flint-inference && sudo systemctl enable --now flint-llamacpp
Roll fwd:   sudo systemctl disable --now flint-llamacpp && sudo systemctl enable --now flint-inference
Status:     systemctl status flint-inference; journalctl -u flint-inference -f
Tuning env (systemctl edit flint-inference): FLINT_NUM_SPEC, FLINT_MAX_MODEL_LEN,
FLINT_MAX_BATCHED, FLINT_PREFIX_CACHING (default --enable-prefix-caching),
FLINT_GPU_UTIL (default 0.97). Context = --max-model-len auto (largest that fits, ~164k tokens with 2048-token prefill chunks).
Experiments: ~/flint-vllm-spike/maintenance.sh stops the active live unit and restarts it on exit.
